# Monocular Visual Odometry with Pose Graph Optimization

A complete, professor-review-grade implementation of a monocular visual odometry pipeline built
from first principles. The system takes a KITTI video sequence as input and outputs a
real-time 3D reconstruction of the environment and an accurate camera trajectory, with
quantitative ATE/RPE evaluation against ground-truth GPS poses.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **KITTI Dataset**: The KITTI Odometry Benchmark sequences are several GB each. The system will
> include an automated download script, but you must have ~5–20 GB free space and run it once
> before the pipeline can execute. Sequence 00 (urban loop, ~4 km) is the recommended starting
> point as it contains loop-closure opportunities.

> [!WARNING]
> **g2o / Pose Graph Optimization Backend**: Native g2o Python bindings (`g2o-python`) can be
> difficult to build/install reliably. The plan handles this with a layered fallback strategy:
> (1) try `g2o-python` via pip, (2) fall back to `graphslam` (pure-Python SE3 graph solver),
> (3) worst case, fall back to `scipy.optimize.least_squares` custom implementation — all three
> implementations of the same Gauss-Newton/Levenberg-Marquardt objective function, so the math
> is identical regardless of which backend loads.

> [!NOTE]
> **Scale Ambiguity**: Monocular VO cannot recover metric scale. We resolve this using the
> known camera height above ground from the KITTI calibration files. This is the same trick
> used in KITTI's own reference implementations and must be documented in the report.

